# Internal reader context for the comprehension layer, and everything written
# *from* it. The reader profile holds Merge4 framing and the never-claim list, and
# the narrative/weekly prose is written against that profile — one essay already
# said "infrastructure vendors like Merge4" by name. This repo publishes to GitHub
# Pages, so all of it stays local.
#
# data/comprehension/threads.json is deliberately NOT ignored: it is news metadata
# plus short movement notes, carries no reader context, and is worth versioning —
# it holds months of thread history that is expensive to rebuild.
config/reader_profile.md
data/comprehension/narratives.json
#data/comprehension/weekly.json
#output/comprehension/

